# A long list of siblings (roadmap os-server.md P15, the kernel's review,
# finding 13): an endpoint copied into every slot of twelve spaces of 256;
# six of the spaces deleted - each slot's delete takes one copy out of the
# endpoint's list of 3,072, at once by its back link - then the endpoint,
# its other 1,536 copies adopted with an interrupt window every 16.
# Interrupts are off longest in a space's retype (call 09: its 8 KB zeroed
# at once), never in a delete or a revoke (before: a delete walked its
# older siblings, and an adoption all the children, in one stretch: the
# longest, a revoke's, near half a tick, past which TEST_STRETCH's measure
# cannot go). tests/programs/additions.asm, TEST_ADD_SIBLINGS; on Bochs,
# whose timing the measure needs.
program: additions
define: TEST_CAPS
define: TEST_ADD_SIBLINGS
define: TEST_STRETCH
emulators: bochs
match: contains
timeout: 180
---
additions: copies made (3072): 3072
additions: half the spaces deleted with them (0): 0
additions: the endpoint deleted (0): 0
additions: done
, at vector 31, call 09
rx286: interrupts never off for 10 ms
